<Layout title="College health membership | Kin & Campus" description="A school-year healthcare program for college students in Blacksburg, with ongoing care, planned check-ins, and 24/7 after-hours guidance for urgent concerns.">
<div class="w ph"><div class="eyebrow">Membership</div><h1>An ongoing healthcare relationship for the school year.</h1><p class="lead">Membership gives a college student an established physician in Blacksburg from August through May. Routine visits, refills, and follow-up are arranged through normal program channels. If an urgent concern arises after hours, guidance is available 24 hours a day, 7 days a week. For a true emergency, call 911 or go to the nearest emergency department.</p></div>
<div class="w">
<div class="notes">
<div class="note-row"><h3>Semester membership</h3><p>Membership costs $800–$1,250 per semester, depending on the level of care needed.</p></div>
<div class="note-row"><h3>What the program includes</h3><p>Membership includes an establishing visit, clinically appropriate follow-up for ongoing concerns, sick visits, prescription management, university forms, and planned check-ins during the academic year. Students also receive guidance in the everyday skills required to manage their own care.</p></div>
<div class="note-row"><h3>How coordination works</h3><p>We learn the student's existing plan and communicate with the hometown physician when it is useful, appropriate, and authorized. Parents may be included according to the adult student's consent.</p></div>
<div class="note-row"><h3>What membership does not replace</h3><p>Students should keep health insurance for laboratory testing, imaging, specialists, emergency care, and hospital services. Membership does not replace 911, an emergency department, or hospital care. After-hours guidance can help a member identify the appropriate next step, but possible emergencies should never wait for a reply.</p></div>
</div>

<div class="eyebrow" style="margin-top:56px">The academic calendar</div>
<h2>Follow-up is planned around predictable changes in routine.</h2>
<p class="lead">College schedules can disrupt medication, sleep, meals, and appointments. We use natural points in the year to review what is working and prepare for what comes next.</p>
<div class="notes">
<div class="note-row"><h3>Move-in and the first weeks</h3><p>Establish the relationship, review current care, arrange appropriate prescriptions, and identify forms or records that need attention.</p></div>
<div class="note-row"><h3>Before and after breaks</h3><p>Confirm medication supply, discuss changes that occurred at home, and make sure the plan still fits the student's routine in Blacksburg.</p></div>
<div class="note-row"><h3>Finals</h3><p>Check on stress, sleep, symptoms, adherence, and prescription needs during a period when students may have less capacity to manage details.</p></div>
<div class="note-row"><h3>End of the school year</h3><p>Review the year's care and coordinate relevant information for summer or continued treatment.</p></div>
</div>

<h2 style="margin:48px 0 20px">Questions about membership</h2>
<details><summary>How does the program begin?</summary><p>A parent or student can request an introductory conversation. We explain the scope of membership and determine whether the student's needs fit the practice. Clinical history and records are handled later through the appropriate secure process.</p></details>
<details><summary>How does access work?</summary><p>Routine care is arranged through normal program channels and the practice's clinical schedule. After-hours guidance for urgent concerns is available 24 hours a day, 7 days a week. Response times can vary, so call 911 or go to the nearest emergency department if the situation may be an emergency.</p></details>
<details><summary>Will you share my student's information with me?</summary><p>An adult student controls their health information. We document what they consent to share and follow those preferences. Safety obligations and other legal requirements still apply.</p></details>
<details><summary>Does this replace insurance?</summary><p>No. Keep the student's primary insurance for services outside the membership, including labs, imaging, specialists, emergency departments, and hospital care.</p></details>
<details><summary>What if my student is away from Blacksburg?</summary><p>The program is centered on local care in Blacksburg. Some follow-up may be appropriate by video, depending on the student's location, clinical need, and applicable requirements.</p></details>
<details><summary>What if it is an emergency?</summary><p>Call 911 or go to the nearest emergency department. Do not wait for a response through routine or after-hours program channels. Once the immediate issue is addressed, Kin &amp; Campus can help with appropriate follow-up and coordination.</p></details>
<p style="margin-top:36px"><a class="btn" href={href("join")}>Request an introduction</a></p>
</div>
</Layout>
